00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.960
- Anyone else we know?
- I met Lucson and Juli.

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:20.030
Really?

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:23.430
Thank you for seeing me off, Pat.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:26.470
Here's a Ralph Lawrence
quality handkerchief.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:29.140
It's a present to you
for coming to see me off.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:32.010
It'll remind you of me while you
devote yourself to your studies...!

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.980
Juli! I'm going, too!

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.520
You have a lot more to learn first.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:43.950
About this world, about society,
and about yourself.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.160
Once you've learned that,
then will you come to the Ryvius?

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.130
But...!

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.490
Ran!

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:06.000
I didn't expect you to come, Brian.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:09.580
I didn't wanna, but my dad got
really angry when I said so.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:11.350
Actually, angry is an understatement.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:14.750
In my case, they treated me as some
sort of tribe hero. I couldn't say "no".

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:18.050
I don't believe it. Am I the only one
who came for the sake of humanity?

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:19.460
Far out!

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.760
What? It's not because
you wanted to see me?

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:23.600
For the sake of our future!

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.620
Well, let's just leave it at that.

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:30.270
- Eins. Are your settings accurate?
- Sorry!

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:33.730
We still have time.
Let's verify them, one at a time.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.880
Hey! I'm told we can see
the Ryvius from here!

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:38.640
- Really?
- On the screen, right?

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:07.060
Pat. Grow up to be a proud Zwei.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:14.800
I'd prefer not to acknowledge it,
but if I was in fact mistaken...

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:16.780
...I need to fix where I erred.
That's why I came.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:20.280
Is that so. Then leave everything to me.

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:23.390
I'll teach you everything
there is to know about being a Zwei.

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:24.660
You will?

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:28.490
Why don't we both study
what we need to know. Both you and I.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.230
Have you lost weight?

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:35.200
You seem to have gained
about 5 percent.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.000
- How dare you!
- I apologize.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:49.550
<i>The connecting hatch</i>
<i>to gate 57 will be opened.</i>

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:53.880
<i>Those who have completed boarding</i>
<i>procedures should proceed onto the ship.</i>

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:56.490
Nicks! Hurry!
They say the hatch is open!

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.560
- <i>The connecting hatch has been opened.</i>
- Wait, Akihiro!

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:00.860
- <i>Those who have completed boarding...!</i>
- You're fast for a fat guy!

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:15.680
- Where's your boyfriend?
- He's too afraid to come.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:16.870
I don't care, anymore!

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.810
The rooms seem to be a lot nicer this time.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.450
And rooms have already been allocated.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:26.690
- Not here, either.
- No.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:29.080
Hey, what do you think Yuki's
doing right about now?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:32.850
Him? Let's see... probably...!

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.150
Where is he? Where the hell is he?

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.130
You're acting like a little kid.

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:42.160
<i>You'd better have the decency to do</i>
<i>a return match. I trust you do, Airs Blue!</i>

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:44.500
Have you made up with him?

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.670
Well, we no longer have
meaningless fights.

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:48.940
Things are a lot better
now than they used to be.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:50.110
I see.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.610
I wish I had the chance like you did,
to make my point clear.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.170
To Kozue... to Reiko...!

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:57.280
I'm sure you'll have the chance.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:01.720
Hi!

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:03.890
Kouji Aiba.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.020
I'm home, Neya.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:07.860
Welcome home.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.560
What do you mean, "I'm home"?

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:12.900
You read the materials, right?
She's the Ryvius's Sphix.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:16.500
Oh! That thing about a section
of the control system taking form.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.840
I wanted to see you, Kouji.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:20.670
Yeah, so did I.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:23.610
Ah, n-not in that way.

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.950
I'm telling ya...
why do I need to explain myself?

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.220
So, what did you do?

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:41.220
All kinds of things.
And I went to the Moon.

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:43.900
But I couldn't see Kozue.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:46.890
I won't ask you what
happened in your past...

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:50.670
...but it's clear that you loved Kozue.

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:53.640
At least I believe you loved her.

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.140
I was just so afraid
to fall in love with her.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:00.340
I kept seeing my sister
and Kozue as one person...

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:03.180
...so I was afraid that if
I fell in love with her...

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:05.940
...she would disappear,
like my sister did.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:07.790
That's why...!

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:11.180
Take it easy.

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.390
The strength of a single
person has its limits.

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:16.490
As long as we do what we can,
however we can, it should be fine.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:21.260
We don't have to grasp our future.
Let's focus on grasping tomorrow.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.030
I believe that's plenty.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.680
- What's your problem?
- How about apologizing?

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:31.140
I apologized!

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:33.910
Let's go. Let's go.

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:38.850
- Cut it out!
- Hey!

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:45.920
<i>You know, I think, that often</i>
<i>things won't go as we wish...</i>

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:49.060
<i>...and almost everyday there's bound</i>
<i>to be something that makes us mad.</i>

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:51.230
<i>There's nothing we can</i>
<i>do to change that flow.</i>

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:53.820
<i>But that's not necessarily true.</i>

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:56.930
<i>There's a need for us to give</i>
<i>these things some thought as well.</i>

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:00.870
<i>A future that we're sitting</i>
<i>back waiting to arrive...</i>

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.440
<i>...doesn't tie us to tomorrow.</i>

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:04.910
<i>And I don't want a tomorrow like that.</i>

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.520
What's bothering you so much
that you can't stop crying, Ran?

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:18.010
No. Nothing at all.

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:20.250
Lucson, please confirm final preparations.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:22.830
You're the captain.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:23.900
Come again?

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:25.670
- There's no reason why not.
- Yeah.

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:27.930
There's no one else here
who wants to take charge.

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:29.840
If it doesn't work out,
we'll deal with it then.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:30.940
It's not gonna work out.

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.810
But you've gotta commit
to at least a month.

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:35.540
- Don't be too unreasonable.
- I'll help out too.

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:37.040
Please, Lucson.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:42.450
Okay. I shall put my experience
as former leader of the Ryvius to use!

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:44.320
Then can you please
make the announcement?

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:49.690
<i>Ah, everybody, I, Lucson Houjou,</i>
<i>will be serving as captain of the Ryvius.</i>

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.990
<i>Wow! I can almost hear</i>
<i>the cheering echo throughout the ship.</i>

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.550
<i>By the way, Juli Bahana</i>
<i>will be serving as sub-commander.</i>

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:58.960
What a relief!

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:02.100
As I expected!

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:03.640
Yes?

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:05.800
<i>Kouji! What happened to your face?</i>

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:08.870
Oh, nothing. What did you want me for?

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:11.510
<i>We haven't decided</i>
<i>on the Ryvius's course yet.</i>

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:13.480
<i>We were hoping that</i>
<i>you could do the honors.</i>

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:15.640
<i>We want you to decide.</i>

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:20.550
Then how about going to see the
people who didn't make the trip here?

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:25.090
We can begin with...
well, how about Uranus's moon, Titania?

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:27.220
- <i>Titania?</i>
- <i>Why?</i>

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.690
There's a person there that I want to see.

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:31.860
There's something
I'd like to discuss with her.

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:34.460
- <i>Very well.</i>
- <i>Then Titania it is.</i>

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:36.260
Thank you.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.500
I have an announcement!

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.530
<i>The Ryvius is now ready to sail!</i>

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:14.940
<i>This ship will be on course</i>
<i>to the vicinity of Uranus!</i>

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:22.480
My, oh my. More scratches and bruises.

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:30.920
Okay! Black Ryvius!
Taking off to Titania!

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.350
Roger, Captain.

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:58.010
Boy, that was painful.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.050
Perhaps we overdid it a bit.

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:02.180
Those guys must've
really hated your guts.

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:03.690
Well, I apologize.

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:05.160
I'm only kidding.

00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:42.060
And then...

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:43.030
And then... One day...

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:47.300
And then... One day... Some time...!

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:02.580
In your dry eyes...

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:07.650
...a silhouette appears

00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:12.360
The blue colored future...

00:22:12.360 --> 00:22:19.090
...swayed and glittered

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:28.510
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:37.120
...freedom out of pity

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:45.560
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:49.460
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:55.830
goodbye
